<h1>MA'AD AHLIL AATHAR Assessment System<br>Firebase Migration Guide</h1>
<p><em>Version 1.0 — May 2026</em></p>

<h2>1. What is Firebase?</h2>
<p>Firebase is Google's backend-as-a-service platform. It provides:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Firebase Authentication</strong> — email/password login, Google login, etc.</li>
<li><strong>Cloud Firestore</strong> — a real-time NoSQL database (replaces IndexedDB)</li>
<li><strong>Firebase Hosting</strong> — deploy your app with one command</li>
<li><strong>Security Rules</strong> — control who can read/write data</li>
</ul>

<div class="note"><strong>Cost:</strong> Firebase has a generous free tier (Spark Plan) — 50K reads/day, 20K writes/day, 10 GB storage. Enough for a small school.</div>

<h2>2. Prerequisites</h2>
<ul>
<li>A Google account (Gmail)</li>
<li>Node.js installed (already have it)</li>
<li>Basic understanding of JavaScript/Promises</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Step-by-Step Migration Plan</h2>

<h3>3.1 Create a Firebase Project</h3>
<ol>
<li>Go to <a href="https://console.firebase.google.com">console.firebase.google.com</a></li>
<li>Click "Add project" → name it <code>maad-sas</code> → follow the prompts</li>
<li>Once created, click the web icon <code>&lt;/&gt;</code> to register your app</li>
<li>Copy the <strong>firebaseConfig</strong> object — you'll need it later</li>
</ol>

<h3>3.2 Enable Authentication</h3>
<ol>
<li>In the Firebase Console, go to "Authentication" → "Sign-in method"</li>
<li>Enable "Email/Password" provider</li>
<li>(Optional) Enable "Google" for Google login</li>
</ol>

<h3>3.3 Create Firestore Database</h3>
<ol>
<li>Go to "Firestore Database" → "Create database"</li>
<li>Choose "Start in test mode" (we'll lock it down later)</li>
<li>Choose a location closest to your users (e.g., <code>eur3</code> for Europe)</li>
</ol>

<h3>3.4 Install Firebase SDK</h3>
<pre>npm install firebase</pre>

<h3>3.5 Create Firebase Configuration File</h3>
<p>Create a new file: <code>src/lib/firebase.js</code></p>
<pre>import { initializeApp } from 'firebase/app';
import { getAuth } from 'firebase/auth';
import { getFirestore } from 'firebase/firestore';

const firebaseConfig = {
  apiKey: "YOUR_API_KEY",
  authDomain: "YOUR_PROJECT.firebaseapp.com",
  projectId: "YOUR_PROJECT_ID",
  storageBucket: "YOUR_PROJECT.appspot.com",
  messagingSenderId: "YOUR_SENDER_ID",
  appId: "YOUR_APP_ID"
};

const app = initializeApp(firebaseConfig);
export const auth = getAuth(app);
export const db = getFirestore(app);
</pre>

<h2>4. Migration Steps</h2>

<h3>4.1 Migrate Authentication (authStore.js)</h3>
<p><strong>File:</strong> <code>src/store/authStore.js</code></p>
<p>Replace the existing login/logout/init logic with Firebase Auth calls:</p>

<h4>Replacement code for authStore.js:</h4>
<pre>import { create } from 'zustand';
import { 
  signInWithEmailAndPassword, 
  signOut, 
  onAuthStateChanged 
} from 'firebase/auth';
import { doc, getDoc, setDoc } from 'firebase/firestore';
import { auth, db } from '../lib/firebase';

const useAuthStore = create((set, get) => ({
  user: null,
  isAuthenticated: false,
  isLoading: true,

  init: () => {
    onAuthStateChanged(auth, async (firebaseUser) => {
      if (firebaseUser) {
        const userDoc = await getDoc(doc(db, 'users', firebaseUser.uid));
        if (userDoc.exists()) {
          set({ user: { id: firebaseUser.uid, ...userDoc.data() }, isAuthenticated: true, isLoading: false });
        } else {
          set({ isLoading: false });
        }
      } else {
        set({ user: null, isAuthenticated: false, isLoading: false });
      }
    });
  },

  login: async (email, password) => {
    const result = await signInWithEmailAndPassword(auth, email, password);
    const userDoc = await getDoc(doc(db, 'users', result.user.uid));
    if (!userDoc.exists()) throw new Error('User profile not found');
    const userData = { id: result.user.uid, ...userDoc.data() };
    set({ user: userData, isAuthenticated: true });
    return userData;
  },

  logout: async () => {
    await signOut(auth);
    set({ user: null, isAuthenticated: false });
  },

  addUser: async (data) => {
    const { createUserWithEmailAndPassword } = await import('firebase/auth');
    const result = await createUserWithEmailAndPassword(auth, data.email, data.password);
    const { password, ...safeData } = data;
    await setDoc(doc(db, 'users', result.user.uid), {
      ...safeData,
      createdAt: new Date().toISOString(),
    });
    return result.user.uid;
  },

  // Keep getUsers, updateUser, deleteUser using Firestore doc operations
  // getUsers: async () => { ... } fetch all docs from 'users' collection
  // updateUser: async (id, data) => { ... } update doc
  // deleteUser: async (id) => { ... } delete doc
}));

export default useAuthStore;</pre>

<h3>4.2 Migrate Database (replace db/database.js)</h3>
<p><strong>File:</strong> <code>src/db/database.js</code> — replace entirely</p>
<p>The current Dexie IndexedDB schema needs to be translated to Firestore collections:</p>

<table>
<tr><th>Dexie Table</th><th>Firestore Collection</th><th>Document ID</th></tr>
<tr><td>users</td><td>users</td><td>Firebase Auth UID</td></tr>
<tr><td>settings</td><td>settings</td><td>"school_settings"</td></tr>
<tr><td>classes</td><td>classes</td><td>auto-generated</td></tr>
<tr><td>students</td><td>students</td><td>auto-generated</td></tr>
<tr><td>subjects</td><td>subjects</td><td>auto-generated</td></tr>
<tr><td>results</td><td>results</td><td>auto-generated</td></tr>
<tr><td>cumulativeAverages</td><td>cumulativeAverages</td><td>auto-generated</td></tr>
<tr><td>promotions</td><td>promotions</td><td>auto-generated</td></tr>
<tr><td>attendance</td><td>attendance</td><td>auto-generated</td></tr>
</table>

<pre>// src/db/database.js — Firestore version
import { db } from '../lib/firebase';

// Helper: convert Firestore collection snapshot to array
const snapshotToArray = (snapshot) => {
  const arr = [];
  snapshot.forEach(doc => arr.push({ id: doc.id, ...doc.data() }));
  return arr;
};

export { db, snapshotToArray };
export default db;</pre>

<h3>4.3 Migrate a Store (Example: studentsStore.js)</h3>
<p><strong>File:</strong> <code>src/store/studentsStore.js</code></p>
<p>Replace Dexie calls with Firestore calls. Here's the pattern for every store:</p>

<pre>import { create } from 'zustand';
import { 
  collection, getDocs, getDoc, doc, addDoc, 
  updateDoc, deleteDoc, query, where, orderBy 
} from 'firebase/firestore';
import { db } from '../lib/firebase';

const useStudentsStore = create((set, get) => ({
  students: [],
  loading: true,

  loadStudents: async () => {
    const snapshot = await getDocs(collection(db, 'students'));
    const students = [];
    snapshot.forEach(d => students.push({ id: d.id, ...d.data() }));
    set({ students, loading: false });
  },

  getStudent: async (id) => {
    const docSnap = await getDoc(doc(db, 'students', String(id)));
    return docSnap.exists() ? { id: docSnap.id, ...docSnap.data() } : null;
  },

  addStudent: async (data) => {
    const docRef = await addDoc(collection(db, 'students'), {
      ...data,
      createdAt: new Date().toISOString(),
    });
    const all = await getDocs(collection(db, 'students'));
    const students = [];
    all.forEach(d => students.push({ id: d.id, ...d.data() }));
    set({ students });
    return docRef.id;
  },

  updateStudent: async (id, data) => {
    await updateDoc(doc(db, 'students', String(id)), data);
    const snapshot = await getDocs(collection(db, 'students'));
    const students = [];
    snapshot.forEach(d => students.push({ id: d.id, ...d.data() }));
    set({ students });
  },

  deleteStudent: async (id) => {
    await deleteDoc(doc(db, 'students', String(id)));
    const snapshot = await getDocs(collection(db, 'students'));
    const students = [];
    snapshot.forEach(d => students.push({ id: d.id, ...d.data() }));
    set({ students });
  },

  bulkAddStudents: async (records) => {
    let success = 0;
    let errors = 0;
    for (const record of records) {
      try {
        await addDoc(collection(db, 'students'), {
          ...record, createdAt: new Date().toISOString(),
        });
        success++;
      } catch { errors++; }
    }
    const snapshot = await getDocs(collection(db, 'students'));
    const students = [];
    snapshot.forEach(d => students.push({ id: d.id, ...d.data() }));
    set({ students });
    return { success, errors };
  },
}));

export default useStudentsStore;</pre>

<h3>4.4 Migrate Settings Store (special case — single document)</h3>
<pre>import { create } from 'zustand';
import { doc, getDoc, setDoc } from 'firebase/firestore';
import { db } from '../lib/firebase';

const defaultSettings = {
  schoolName: "MA'AD AHLIL AATHAR",
  address: 'No 3, Mosadoluwa Street...',
  phones: '08033719211, 08034660100, 08062837011',
  // ... other defaults
};

const useSettingsStore = create((set) => ({
  settings: null,
  loading: true,

  loadSettings: async () => {
    const docSnap = await getDoc(doc(db, 'settings', 'school_settings'));
    if (docSnap.exists()) {
      set({ settings: docSnap.data(), loading: false });
    } else {
      await setDoc(doc(db, 'settings', 'school_settings'), defaultSettings);
      set({ settings: defaultSettings, loading: false });
    }
  },

  updateSettings: async (data) => {
    await setDoc(doc(db, 'settings', 'school_settings'), data);
    set({ settings: data });
  },
}));

export default useSettingsStore;</pre>

<h2>5. Database Conversion Script</h2>
<p>To migrate existing data from IndexedDB to Firestore, create a one-time script:</p>
<pre>// src/lib/migrateToFirebase.js
import { collection, addDoc } from 'firebase/firestore';
import { db as firestoreDb } from './firebase';
import localDb from '../db/database';

export async function migrateLocalData() {
  const tables = ['users', 'settings', 'classes', 'students', 'subjects', 'results', 'cumulativeAverages', 'promotions', 'attendance'];
  
  for (const table of tables) {
    const data = await localDb.table(table).toArray();
    for (const item of data) {
      const { id, ...rest } = item;
      if (table === 'settings') {
        await setDoc(doc(firestoreDb, 'settings', 'school_settings'), rest);
      } else {
        await addDoc(collection(firestoreDb, table), rest);
      }
    }
    console.log(`Migrated ${data.length} records from ${table}`);
  }
  alert('Migration complete!');
}</pre>

<h2>6. Security Rules</h2>
<p>In Firebase Console → Firestore → Rules, set these rules:</p>
<pre>rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    // Admin can read/write everything
    match /{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if request.auth != null 
        && request.auth.uid != null;
    }
    
    // Users can only read their own profile
    match /users/{userId} {
      allow read: if request.auth != null 
        && request.auth.uid == userId;
      allow write: if request.auth != null 
        && request.auth.token.role == 'admin';
    }
  }
}</pre>

<h2>7. Deployment</h2>
<ol>
<li>Install Firebase CLI: <code>npm install -g firebase-tools</code></li>
<li>Login: <code>firebase login</code></li>
<li>Init: <code>firebase init</code> → select Hosting → choose <code>dist/</code> as public directory</li>
<li>Build: <code>npm run build</code></li>
<li>Deploy: <code>firebase deploy</code></li>
<li>Your app is live at <code>https://YOUR_PROJECT.web.app</code></li>
</ol>

