<h2>9. Estimated Effort</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Beginner developer:</strong> 1-2 weeks, following this guide step by step</li>
<li><strong>Experienced developer:</strong> 2-3 days</li>
<li><strong>Hiring a developer:</strong> ~$500-1500 USD depending on location and expertise</li>
</ul>

<div class="warn"><strong>Warning:</strong> Firestore charges per read/write/delete operation. The current app loads all data at once — for a school with 500+ students, you may hit Firestore quotas quickly. Consider adding pagination or optimizing queries after migration.</div>

<h2>10. Common Errors & Solutions</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Error</th><th>Solution</th></tr>
<tr><td>Firebase: Error (auth/operation-not-allowed)</td><td>Enable Email/Password sign-in in Firebase Console → Authentication</td></tr>
<tr><td>Missing or insufficient permissions</td><td>Set your Firestore rules to test mode temporarily or check your security rules</td></tr>
<tr><td>Firebase App named '[DEFAULT]' already exists</td><td>Wrap initializeApp in a check: <code>if (!getApps().length) initializeApp(config)</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>getDoc is not a function</td><td>Make sure you imported from 'firebase/firestore', not 'firebase/app'</td></tr>
</table>

